  "id": "DrugBank_DB00266 - MONDO_5068",
  "verbalization": "Dicoumarol is implicated in the pathogenesis of Myocardial Infarction (disease) through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Dicoumarol is associated with Coronary Thrombosis, a condition that leads to the formation of blood clots in the coronary arteries. These clots can result in Myocardial Infarction when they rupture and cause ischemia. The evidence also indicates that Coronary Thrombosis is linked to Phenprocoumon, a drug that is a known antagonist of vitamin K, and that Phenprocoumon, in turn, is associated with Myocardial Infarction. This creates a chain of indications that links Dicoumarol to the development of coronary thrombosis, which ultimately contributes to myocardial infarction. The integration of these pathways highlights a mechanism by which Dicoumarol may be associated with myocardial infarction, emphasizing the role of thrombosis in the disease process.",
